WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:03.086
Cyberpunk is dark,

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:04.713
it's brutal,

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.007
it's hopeless,

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.260
but it's also a really cool way

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.387
for us to think about
what our future could look like.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.765
And you might think of it as just fiction.

00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:20.228
But in the last couple of years, you've
seen just how fast things can change

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:23.815
in ways that we would have never
even been able to guess.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:25.900
Let's try to look at Cyberpunk

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.862
from an architecture and urban planning
point of view to see

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:34.284
is it just fiction or
is there a real connection to our reality?

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.328
Are we already dreaming of electric sheep?

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:40.874
A portion of this video

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:44.794
is sponsored by NordVPN.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:48.715
Cyberpunk is a subgenre
of science fiction, but it focuses

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:53.094
on the darker side of technology,
often bleak dystopian futures.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:56.806
You have a technological, advanced, yet
declining society

00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.435
where people constantly struggle
to maintain a sense of self

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:03.396
in the face of technology
that's becoming so superior.

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:06.399
It's typically set in a dark, urbanized

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:10.153
and globalized world
with a gritty underground

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:13.990
subculture, with things
like cyborgs, virtual reality, A.I.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.492
and cybernetic implants.

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:22.123
Big corporations control everything, and
technology is both a lifeline and a leash.

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:24.250
It's what you need to survive.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.961
And yet it's the tool that controls them.

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:28.505
Say something nice.

00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:34.302
One of the key features of a

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:37.889
cyberpunk city
is the density and complexity.

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:41.101
We have towering skyscrapers,

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.728
usually overpopulated and polluted.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:47.107
We have labyrinthine streets and alleyways
and a vast

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.359
network of interconnected technologies.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:57.617
It's basically an urban jungle
where people are forced

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:01.663
to navigate a complex
and dangerous landscape to survive.

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:06.459
But at the same time, cyberpunk
cities can be places of opportunity

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:11.339
and possibility where the marginalized
can carve out a niche for themselves.

00:02:11.339 --> 00:02:16.302
And so I don't think it's an accident
that the most common recurring cities in

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.389
cyberpunk are set in cities like Tokyo,

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:22.392
L.A., Hong Kong or London, North America.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:25.311
It's the place of hope,
the American dream,

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:30.191
but it's also an icon of capitalism
and Asia.

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:33.194
Super dense,
technologically advanced cities.

00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:35.989
But there's a lot of uncertainty
about the future.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.950
But there's another more obvious reason.

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:43.329
Cyberpunk emerged in the eighties
and nineties, where the U.S.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:46.708
and Japan were at the forefront
of technological innovation.

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:49.502
We saw the rise of Silicon Valley

00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:52.714
as well as the rise of Japan's
tech industry.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:57.969
So these areas became associated with
cutting edge technological development.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:02.891
And so it served as a natural backdrop
for these cyberpunk stories.

00:03:13.818 --> 00:03:14.861
Okay, stop.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.781
In the original Ghost in the Shell,
there's

00:03:18.781 --> 00:03:23.369
only one scene where you can obviously
distinguish kids in the environment.

00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:27.957
Having children in cities is not just
important for social stability,

00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:33.046
economic growth, cultural continuity,
but also for urban planning.

00:03:33.796 --> 00:03:36.841
They bring life and energy
to public spaces.

00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:41.346
They bring spontaneity and play and fun
and in fact,

00:03:41.638 --> 00:03:45.183
public spaces that are designed
with kids at the forefront.

00:03:45.516 --> 00:03:48.728
It can actually lead
to a more vibrant space for everyone.

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:53.858
Just look at this project Superkilen
in Denmark by Bjarke Ingels Architects.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.695
Instead of creating isolated
playgrounds for kids,

00:03:57.946 --> 00:04:01.532
they integrated the play areas
within the larger public realm.

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:05.036
And by doing that,
they made the entire area

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:10.625
more interactive, more inclusive, more
accessible, and more fun for everyone.

00:04:15.171 --> 00:04:17.465
The absence of children in cyberpunk

00:04:17.715 --> 00:04:21.261
is a very obvious
in the design of these cities,

00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:23.346
and it just speaks to a society

00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:27.225
that's not only struggling with crime
or cost of living,

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:32.230
but also a society that has no hope
and no vision for the future.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.357
And this isn't just fiction.

00:04:34.816 --> 00:04:36.985
Places like Japan and Korea,

00:04:36.985 --> 00:04:40.738
they're already experiencing
a pretty scary birth decline.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:44.575
And you can actually see how that's
already impacting the economy

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:46.119
and the real estate market.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:49.622
The problems are obviously pretty complex
and there's a lot of factors

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:53.668
that go into it
like the kind of social tolerance

00:04:53.668 --> 00:04:56.796
to completely
shutting yourself off from society.

00:04:57.588 --> 00:05:00.383
But it could also simply be

00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:04.137
that the lifestyles are really demanding
and the long

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:07.807
working hours just leave
very little time for personal life.

00:05:08.516 --> 00:05:11.477
That plus the rising cost of living.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:15.523
It's not really the ideal condition
for starting a family.

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.775
Whatever is the crux of the problem.

00:05:17.775 --> 00:05:22.030
If this continues to happen
in the next couple of generations,

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:26.075
we're probably going to be seeing
what we're seeing in these dystopian

00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:27.076
cyberpunk worlds.

