00:11:29.105 --> 00:11:30.648
In both of the Blade Runner movies,

00:11:30.648 --> 00:11:34.151
there's lots of great examples of what
you will call brutalist architecture.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:39.073
Brutalism emerged in the 1950s,
and when Philip K Dick wrote

00:11:39.156 --> 00:11:42.368
Do Androids
Dream of Electric Sheep in 1961,

00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:45.162
which is the book
that Blade Runner was based on.

00:11:45.162 --> 00:11:49.333
Brutalism was thought
to be futuristic ahead of its time,

00:11:49.417 --> 00:11:51.752
and actually it was considered
kind of radical,

00:11:52.044 --> 00:11:55.005
especially compared to the smooth, clean,

00:11:55.005 --> 00:11:58.259
sterile quality of modernism,
which came before it.

00:11:58.342 --> 00:12:03.556
It was even considered a socialist form
of architecture, these bare structures.

00:12:03.931 --> 00:12:07.601
The idea was that
they provided a kind of blank canvas

00:12:07.601 --> 00:12:10.479
that could be influenced
by people's experiences over time.

00:12:10.604 --> 00:12:13.482
It was the kind of architecture
that instead of saying,

00:12:13.733 --> 00:12:17.820
Look at me,
it came alive only by involving people.

00:12:18.195 --> 00:12:23.659
It was democratic,
it was social, and it was morally right.

00:12:25.202 --> 00:12:27.288
Or that was the idea.

00:12:27.288 --> 00:12:28.205
Just look at this.

00:12:28.205 --> 00:12:32.293
Concrete deteriorates and weathers
really badly over time,

00:12:33.002 --> 00:12:35.504
despite these grand social visions.

00:12:35.796 --> 00:12:38.507
It turns out people don't actually like

00:12:38.507 --> 00:12:41.594
hanging out
in these massive raw concrete spaces.

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:45.055
So eventually these buildings
became neglected.

00:12:45.598 --> 00:12:48.184
But the problem was
because these buildings are just

00:12:48.184 --> 00:12:50.978
so massive and dense with concrete,

00:12:51.353 --> 00:12:55.316
apparently it will create a huge amount
of carbon footprint and demolish it.

00:12:55.858 --> 00:12:59.236
So we're stuck with these cold, raw,

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:01.906
concrete monsters.

