00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:31.263
So when we cover of the building's facades
with ads,

00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:35.225
it takes away the unique character
or the spirit of that place.

00:15:35.559 --> 00:15:40.105
And we start to lose identity, not just in
our cities, but also in ourselves.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:46.612
A public square is a space that's owned
and maintained

00:15:46.612 --> 00:15:50.616
by the government or a public entity,
and it's accessible to everyone.

00:15:50.741 --> 00:15:54.078
Public squares are considered
to be a part of the public domain,

00:15:54.078 --> 00:15:58.415
and they're governed by laws
that regulate the use of public spaces.

00:15:58.415 --> 00:16:03.045
In contrast, a privately owned
square is a space that's owned

00:16:03.045 --> 00:16:08.550
and maintained by a private individual
or a company or an organization.

00:16:08.926 --> 00:16:10.678
These spaces are typically located

00:16:10.678 --> 00:16:14.098
on private property, like a shopping mall
or a corporate campus.

00:16:14.473 --> 00:16:17.184
And although they might feel public,

00:16:17.476 --> 00:16:22.356
they're actually only accessible to people
who are permitted to enter the property.

