it's not actually a public space.

00:16:31.615 --> 00:16:37.162
If you linger for too long
or you look like a unsavory character,

00:16:37.663 --> 00:16:41.208
or you're just a demographic
that's not deemed desirable,

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.877
they're in their full rights
to kick you out.

00:16:44.545 --> 00:16:49.383
So when our public spaces start
to get taken over by private interests.

00:16:49.633 --> 00:16:53.971
In the end, they can set the rules
and it might not seem like a big deal

00:16:54.346 --> 00:16:55.431
until it is,

00:16:56.765 --> 00:16:59.893
for example, Zuccotti Park or Liberty
Plaza

00:16:59.893 --> 00:17:04.356
Park in New York
City is a privately owned public space.

00:17:04.565 --> 00:17:07.401
And in 2011,
it was the site of Occupy Wall Street

00:17:07.443 --> 00:17:11.905
where protesters camped out
for several weeks for a peaceful protest.

00:17:12.114 --> 00:17:15.284
But in November 2011,
the protesters were evicted,

00:17:15.576 --> 00:17:19.121
although it wasn't their full
right of free speech and assembly,

00:17:19.288 --> 00:17:23.000
because the owner of the space, Brookfield
Properties,

00:17:23.292 --> 00:17:26.295
allegedly complained to the city
about them

00:17:26.295 --> 00:17:27.546
being there.

00:17:30.257 --> 00:17:33.093
Abolish all forms of rent control,

00:17:33.302 --> 00:17:36.221
abolish all forms of social

00:17:36.346 --> 00:17:39.850
and affordable housing, privatize

00:17:39.933 --> 00:17:44.313
all street squares, public spaces

00:17:44.313 --> 00:17:47.608
and parks, whole urban districts.

00:17:48.192 --> 00:17:51.445
These are not the government
mandates of a cyberpunk movie.

00:17:51.695 --> 00:17:55.491
This is directly
pulled from the eight point manifesto

00:17:55.491 --> 00:18:00.621
or proposed by a prominent partner
at Zaha Hadid Architects,

00:18:00.788 --> 00:18:04.792
one of the most well-known
